From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kboot: Reserve the trust cache

On t8132 (M4), the trust cache that iBoot lists in
/chosen/memory-map lies inside the usable RAM range handed to the
kernel, so Linux may allocate from and write to it.

Add a /memreserve/ entry for it, as for the SMP-RO area, so the kernel
keeps it mapped but never allocates from it. Where the trust cache is
outside the usable range the entry has no effect.

This replaces the kernel-side ADT parser that Omarchy-M4-Native carried
for the same purpose.
---
--- a/src/kboot.c
+++ b/src/kboot.c
@@ -2817,6 +2817,15 @@
             bail("FDT: couldn't add reservation for M4+ SMP-RO CTRR area\n");
     }
 
+    // On M4, iBoot leaves the trust cache inside the usable RAM range.
+    int anode_mmap = adt_path_offset(adt, "/chosen/memory-map");
+    u64 trust_cache[2];
+    if (anode_mmap >= 0 &&
+        ADT_GETPROP_ARRAY(adt, anode_mmap, "TrustCache", trust_cache) == sizeof(trust_cache)) {
+        if (fdt_add_mem_rsv(dt, trust_cache[0], trust_cache[1]))
+            bail("FDT: couldn't add reservation for the trust cache\n");
+    }
+
     /* setup console log buffer early to capture as much log as possible */
     dt_setup_mtd_phram();
 
